# Developer-evidence exception record — template only (does not take effect
# until it is at .data-quality-gate/change.yaml on the PR branch, per
# .claude/skills/data-quality-gate/reference/evidence-exception.md). No Data
# Team approval is required for this file to pass the gate; the gate
# verifies only that `affected_objects[].before`/`after` match the actual
# detected diff exactly. Narrative fields are presence-checked, not proven true.

purpose: >
  One or two sentences: why this destructive/narrowing change is intentional
  and safe.
ticket: "JIRA-1234"

affected_objects:
  - table: users
    column: legacy_phone
    change_type: REMOVED          # must match the gate's own classification exactly
    before:
      type: text
      nullable: true
    after: null

reason: >
  Why the removal/truncation/regression is intentional (e.g. "column
  deprecated in JIRA-1234, replaced by phone_e164, dual-write completed
  2026-08-01").

dependency_scan: >
  What was checked to confirm no live consumer still reads this
  object (grep results, service inventory, etc.) — free text, presence-
  checked only.

archive_evidence: >
  Where the pre-change data is archived/backed up (path, snapshot ID,
  retention policy reference) — free text, presence-checked only.

validation_evidence: >
  How you confirmed the migration/data change behaves as intended
  (reconciliation query results, row counts before/after, etc.) — free
  text, presence-checked only.

recovery_plan: >
  Exact steps to roll forward or restore if this change turns out to be
  wrong in production — free text, presence-checked only.

attestation:
  owner: "your-name@your-org.com"
  date: "2026-09-02"
  statement: >
    I am the developer/remediation owner for this change and attest the
    above is accurate to the best of my knowledge.
